  "query_preview": "..The large scale shows a trough to our west across the \nwestern Great Basin and California, an upper low tracking northeast \nacross eastern Nevada and a ridge of high pressure centered over \nTexas. The flow across southeast Arizona between the trough to the \nwest and the upper high to the east is southerly and PWAT's are \ncurrently in the 0.85 to 1.0 inch range across much of the forecast \narea (with lesser amounts of around 0.65 inches over far western \nPima County and the White Mountains of northern Greenlee County). \n\nThe current forecast has a chance of showers and thunderstorms from \nSells eastward today, with the highest POPs over Cochise, Graham and \nGreenlee counties. The U of A WRF model and other high res models \nfavor the International Border and eastern counties this afternoon \nand evening. PWAT's are expected to climb into the 1.1 to 1.3 range \nlate this afternoon and evening. WPC has the eastern two-thirds of \nsoutheast Arizona highlighted in a MRGL risk today, with a SLGT risk \nright along the New Mexico state line and points eastward. \n\nOverall, forecast looks on track. No updates this morning to the \ngrids or text products. Main threats from storms today will be heavy \nrainfall, with a secondary threat of gusty outflows with the \nstrongest storms. For more information on the latter periods of the \nforecast, please refer to the PREV DISCUSSION section below.",
